# ==========================================
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS
# ==========================================
# TypeScript's incremental build cache. Nothing depends on it (deleting it only
# makes the next `tsc` slower), and it is rewritten by every typecheck, so a
# tracked copy would leave every working tree permanently dirty.
# It was tracked until the Phase 21–26 release baseline, which removed it from the
# index (`git rm --cached`) so this rule finally applies to it. The file itself is
# NOT deleted — it stays on disk and is still rewritten by every typecheck.
*.tsbuildinfo
# Emitted by `next dev`/`next build`. The Next.js TypeScript docs are explicit:
# "next-env.d.ts is managed by Next.js... Add it to .gitignore. If your project already
# tracks the file, remove it from Git. Do not edit this file manually."
# (node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/05-config/02-typescript.md §next-env.d.ts)
# Untracked at the same time and for the same reason as the build cache above; still
# generated on disk by the build, just no longer versioned.
next-env.d.ts

# ==========================================
# RUNTIME STATE (never source)
# ==========================================
# Default `UPLOAD_DIR` (`lib/images/process.ts`, `app/api/uploads/events/[filename]/route.ts`).
# This holds processed event imagery uploaded by organizers at run time — binary content
# that grows without bound, is specific to one deployment, and is backed up as data (see
# .env.example). It must never be committed, and it is the directory the application WRITES.
#storage/

# WhatsApp auth state (legacy)
#data/whatsapp-auth/
